# Docs pattern

**Voice:** Follow **[.cursor/rules/voice-tone.mdc](voice-tone.mdc)**.

## Stack

- Markdown under `docs/` built with **Zensical + Patina**.
- Nav order lives only in `zensical.toml` — never number filenames.
- Read `.kiro/steering/docs-pattern.md` and `source-lock.md` before inventing procedure detail.

## Page shape

1. One H1.
2. Short lede.
3. Numbered steps or symptom table.
4. Screenshot placeholders → fill during live setup (`docs/assets/images/`).
5. Link to the next nav page.

## Command + result cards

Match the [route53 profiles](https://aws-route53-central-outbound.johna.kiwi/demo/profiles/) pattern — one `.run` card per command, result in a separate `text {.no-copy}` fence:

````markdown
<div class="run" markdown>

```bash
lsusb | grep -i espressif
```

```text {.no-copy}
Bus 003 Device 006: ID 303a:1001 Espressif USB JTAG/serial debug unit
```

</div>
````

Do not put the command and its stdout in one fence. Do not stack unrelated commands in one card.

## Tables

Use spaced GFM separators:

```markdown
| Column A | Column B |
| --- | --- |
| one | two |
```

## Critical hardware rules

- Target **Heltec v4** only in this walkthrough.
- Role: **Companion · Bluetooth** (`companionBle`) for the phone path.
- Bootloader before web flash: hold USER (PRG), tap RST, release USER.
- Web Serial: Chrome / Chromium / Edge only.
- Set radio preset before TX (**New Zealand (Narrow)** for NZ).
- MeshCore ≠ Meshtastic — they do not interoperate on air.

## Accuracy

Prefer facts in `.kiro/steering/source-lock.md`. Tag anything not yet observed as **unverified**.
